                <pb facs="0550" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1115/3961: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-15T13:00:00+01:00">August 15, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 15—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>332. My 323, August 5, 1 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d515-f1"/> Cuban Consul Abela
                    here this morning. He says most “Cubans” are really Spanish but born by chance
                    in Cuba and under Cuban laws Cuban citizens. He say his purpose is to send those
                    brought out by us into rebel territory. This latter purpose in my opinion
                    gravely compromises our record of absolute neutrality if Valencia hears and any
                    of the Cubans are of military age. Since the <hi rendition="#italic">Kane</hi>
                    will probably return from Santander before going to Gijon you have time to
                    consider this new phase.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
